Keep audio decoder chatter out of the log at the default levels.

Why: while Library Management analyses a library (ReplayGain, AcoustID
fingerprints), symphonia logs one INFO line per damaged MP3 frame ("count1
overrun, malformed bitstream") and a WARN per odd ID3 frame ("invalid language
code"): measured 2026-10-24, 28,335 lines and 4.2 MB in 10 minutes from one
pod, none a person can act on, all shipped to VictoriaLogs. LOG_LEVEL now adds
`symphonia=error,lofty=error`; RUST_LOG still replaces the whole filter.

Tests: config tests pass (21) with the updated expectation; a new test pins the
default and DEBUG filters (cargo test -p droppedneedle-kernel --lib config).

Remove when: upstream quiets the decoders itself.

